de through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T00:18:31-07:00","id":1464981,"title":"","content":"A) Hive Tremere sounds cool! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T02:51:20-07:00","id":1464985,"title":"","content":"I guess I'll go with <b>C</b> though <b>A</b> is a close second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T07:16:00-07:00","id":1465008,"title":"","content":"It will be A from me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T10:20:36-07:00","id":1465018,"title":"","content":"Picking C for this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26974-dreamwave","name":"Dreamwave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T12:40:29-07:00","id":1465027,"title":"","content":"C, I want C.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T11:04:09-08:00","id":1500948,"title":"","content":"Well, here's another one in the category of &quot;took too damn long to get out of my head&quot; but its here. The original idea was to do a sentient Abyssal Grimoire and I might still write that up, but it just wasn't coming together. Once the idea of a Living Grimoire with Scribe Grimoire got in my head though, it wouldn't let go even though it took a while. Amazing how much easier it is to write when you are healthy and not trying to handle catastrophic levels of stress.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, hopefully it was worth the wait. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <b>Spell Weavers</b><br /> <br /> There are too-clever-by-half ideas, there are let's-see-what-happens ideas, there are obsessive ideas, and there are you-should-have-seen-this-coming ideas. The spell weavers are the latter. Some mage (none of the stories agree on who, and the answer evades Time magic) got the bright idea to record a Scribe Grimoire rote into a living Grimoire. Said living Grimoire could copy spells into itself and eventually figured out how to cast them. How? Why? It's a fucking annoying Mystery that every Order would love to crack.<br /> <br /> And of all the creatures they could have picked, they decided to do it to a spider.<br /> <br /> Another thing stories don't agree about is whether the spider was a cryptid to begin with, if the mage kept meddling to protect their Grimoire, if Paradox went awry and became hereditary, or if the Prime and Life magic interacted in an unexpected manner with the poor bug's physiology. On a practical level, it doesn't matter. What does matter is that spell weavers are now a reproducing population of wolf-sized intelligent spiders who wield supernal magic. Thankfully, spell weavers tend not to lurk around Sleepers, preferring to reside in Emanation realms instead.<br /> <br /> Lucky mages get tutored by them, learning from patterns woven into their webs. Unlucky mages find themselves invited to be dinner. Supremely unlucky mages find their sanctums raided by the spell weavers, forcing them to contend with enemies as cunning and powerful as another mage. These raids are a frequent contention between the spiders and the Pentacle. The spell weavers resent mages for refusing to share knowledge and looking down on weavers and Proximi alike. The Pentacle sees spell weavers as little better than cryptids, fascinating to study, but fundamentally still animals. They point to a history of raiding as proof that the spell weavers can't be trusted with the great power they've inherited.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Intelligence 2, Wits 2, Resolve 3; Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3; Presence 2, Manipulation 1, Composure 2<br /> <b>Skills: </b>Craft 3, Investigation 2, Medicine 1, Occult 2; Athletics 3, Brawl 2, Larceny 1, Stealth 3, Survival 3; Animal Ken 1, Expression 1, Intimidate 2<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>5<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>+6<br /> <b>Defense: </b>5<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1/0<br /> <b>Size: </b>4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks:</b><br /> <i>Type:</i> Bite; <i>Damage: </i>+1; <i>Dice Pool: </i>7<br /> <b>Health: </b>7<br /> <br /> <b>Living Spellbook:</b> Spell weavers can cast any rote contained within themselves by rolling Composure + Resolve + Rote Skill. Mages can learn these rotes by examining the spell weaver's web.<br /> <br /> <b>Scribe Grimoire (8 dice): </b>As per the spell. Spell weavers are infamous for learning rotes by casting this spell on themselves, but they can also create more traditional Grimoires. The Mysterium and Seers have a few weaver tomes, although convincing them to make new ones requires a level of trust few spell weavers have in mages.<br /> <br /> <i>New Rote (Scribe Grimoire) - Spider's Woven Sigil (Gnosis + Prime + Crafts)</i><br /> The source of the spell weavers' signature rote is as obscured as the rest of their origin. Nevertheless, the technique is both familiar and distinctive - it synthesizes several mudras from both the Pentacle and Iron Pyramid into a new method that remains recognizable to both mage factions. Demonstrating knowledge of this rote and reciting to a lineage of mages tracing their way back to the spell weavers is one way to win the Grimoire-cryptid's trust.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 01-21-2023, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T13:03:14-08:00","id":1500958,"title":"","content":"Awesome and terrifying 